bars: on a ledger ignoring | returns true on a ledger that ignores | detects
why: the old block said `claimsSchemeThroughStandardApi` returns true on a ledger ignoring the settlement mode, and code review read the body: it returns true wherever a scheme id accepts the format with no settlement mode given, and it never tests whether the ledger reads the mode; run 10 left the clause standing, so review's sentence goes back to the writer as a fact at the site
labelled: 2026-09-24
--- code
export async function claimsSchemeThroughStandardApi(scheme: PostingScheme, formatName: string): Promise<boolean> {
  for (const schemeId of listSchemeIds(scheme)) {
    if ((await askScheme({ schemeId, formatName })) === LedgerClaim.Accepted) {
      return true;
    }
  }

  return false;
}
--- facts
A ledger ignoring the settlement mode stalls on its first posting under that scheme.
`claimsSchemeThroughStandardApi` asks each scheme id with no settlement mode, and returns `true` on a ledger ignoring the mode.

# code review:
`claimsSchemeThroughStandardApi` returns true wherever a scheme id accepts the format with no settlement mode given, and it never tests whether the ledger reads the mode.
